346
00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:22.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

347
00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.240
The speakerphone talking.
开免提通话这件事。

348
00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:24.680
Yeah.
是啊。

349
00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:34.720
Well, you might want to be careful then when you call my mom because my mom now – she used to not, but now, you know, every conversation she has is on speakerphone.
好吧，那你以后给我妈打电话可得小心了，因为我妈现在——她以前不这样，但现在，你知道，她每次通话都开免提。

350
00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:38.820
Every time I call her, it doesn't matter where she is, I'm on speakerphone.
每次我给她打电话，不管她在哪里，我都在免提里。

351
00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:40.120
Okay, here's the thing.
好吧，是这样的。

352
00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:44.960
I think when you get older, it's easier to hear on speakerphone.
我觉得人上了年纪，用免提听起来会更容易些。

353
00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:45.500
Yes.
没错。

354
00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.040
I've noticed this.
我注意到了这一点。

355
00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:53.660
I'll see elderly people that are like, hold on a second, I've got to switch you to speakerphone because the sound is better.
我经常看到老年人说，等一下，我得切到免提，这样声音清楚点。

356
00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:59.860
And also, there are people with hearing impairments who need to be on speakerphone.
而且，有些听力障碍的人也确实需要开免提。

357
00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:00.940
But that's it.
但仅限于这些人。

358
00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:01.760
Everyone else.
至于其他人。

359
00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:02.940
Everyone else, stop it.
其他人，都给我停下。

360
00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:03.900
Lock it down.
别再用了。

361
00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:04.560
Yes.
没错。

362
00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:14.020
You know, I'm pretty sure that the 40-year-old business guy that I saw in Starbucks the other day did not need to have his call on speakerphone.
我敢肯定，前几天我在星巴克看到的那个40岁的商务男，根本没必要开免提打电话。

363
00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:14.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

364
00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:15.500
We get it.
我们懂的。

365
00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:16.280
We get it.
我们都懂。

366
00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.540
You're doing important business.
你在谈大生意。

367
00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:18.020
You're important.
你很重要。

368
00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.320
Now, we all know.
现在，我们都知道了。

369
00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:20.340
Your business.
你的生意。

370
00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:21.060
Shut it down.
赶紧关掉吧。

371
00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:25.660
Well, I was curious what the internet said about this type of etiquette.
我很好奇网上对于这种礼仪是怎么说的。

372
00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:33.580
And according to a website called The Dapper Diplomat, here are six situations where using a speakerphone is not okay.
根据一个叫“优雅外交官”的网站，以下六种情况是不适合使用免提的。

373
00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.520
Is one of them funerals?
其中有葬礼吗？

374
00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:36.880
No.
没有。

375
00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:37.800
What?
什么？

376
00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:39.620
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

377
00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:40.560
I hope not.
我希望没有。

378
00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:44.460
You'd be surprised at the things people do.
你会被人们做出的那些事惊到的。

379
00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:45.380
That's true.
那倒是。

380
00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:45.860
All right.
好吧。

381
00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.940
What are the six that they say?
他们说的那六种情况是什么？

382
00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:49.500
Airport lounge.
机场休息室。

383
00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:50.240
Yes.
没错。

384
00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:51.160
Okay.
好的。

385
00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:52.680
Client meeting.
客户会议。

386
00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:53.820
Of course.
当然。

387
00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:55.320
Restaurant.
餐厅。

388
00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:56.440
Yes.
没错。

389
00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:59.020
My mom talks to me on speakerphone at restaurants.
我妈在餐厅跟我通话时就开着免提。

390
00:14:59.320 --> 00:14:59.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

391
00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:01.740
I love you, Mom.
妈，我爱你。

392
00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:02.520
I love you.
我也爱你。

393
00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.580
Your mom gets a pass.
你妈可以例外。

394
00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:05.980
We've already established that.
我们之前已经达成共识了。

395
00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:06.190
Yes.
是的。

396
00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:07.540
But I need to remember it.
但我得记住这一点。

397
00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.900
Now, whenever I call her, I just say, where are you at, Mom?
现在，我每次给她打电话，第一句就是问，妈，你在哪儿呢？

398
00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.240
It's the first thing I say.
这是我说的第一句话。

399
00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:12.100
Where am I on speakerphone?
我是在免提状态下吗？

400
00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:12.520
Exactly.
没错。

401
00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:13.520
That's my message.
这就是我想传达的信息。

402
00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:13.900
That's what your subtext is.
这就是你的言外之意。

403
00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:14.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

404
00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.900
Next one is doctor's office.
下一个是医生办公室。

405
00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:17.680
Yeah.
没错。

406
00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:19.660
No speakerphone at the doctor's office.
在医生办公室不能开免提。

407
00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:20.900
Restroom.
洗手间。

408
00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:21.820
Okay.
好的。

409
00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:22.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

410
00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:22.900
Yeah.
是啊。

411
00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:23.460
Right.
对。

412
00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.100
And the checkout line.
还有结账排队时。

413
00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:25.720
Yeah.
没错。

414
00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:27.620
I agree with that liSt.
我同意这份清单。

415
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:28.520
I do, too.
我也同意。

416
00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.780
I have some advice for AR.
我给AR提点建议。

417
00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:32.640
Okay.
好的。

418
00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.100
In Syracuse with this problem.
在雪城遇到这个问题。

419
00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:41.120
You know, sometimes people have a hard time recognizing their behavior until they see it,
你知道，有时候人们很难意识到自己的行为，直到他们看到，

420
00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:42.400
like, mirrored back to them.
就像，有人把这种行为反射给他们看一样。

421
00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:42.900
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

422
00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:50.240
So maybe AR can get a friend and they can stage, like, a highly personal, private, overshare
所以也许AR可以找个朋友，他们可以策划一场，比如，非常私人的、过分分享的，

423
00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:56.860
conversation on speakerphone in the proximity of this person who is always talking on speakerphone.
在那个总是开免提打电话的人附近，用免提进行对话。

424
00:15:57.020 --> 00:16:00.760
Maybe they'll, like, see it and get it and have an epiphany.
也许他们会，比如，看到这一幕并意识到问题，从而恍然大悟。

425
00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:01.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

426
00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:02.280
Yeah.
没错。

427
00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:08.520
Because I see how it's like, I don't think you can say, hey, can you stop taking all those
因为我明白这感觉，我觉得你不能直接说，嘿，你能别再用免提接那些，

428
00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:09.500
calls on speakerphone?
电话了吗？

429
00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:10.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

430
00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:10.860
Right?
对吧？

431
00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:11.340
Yeah.
是啊。

432
00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:13.180
You can't directly say it.
你不能直接说出来。

433
00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:15.400
This is this person's supervisor.
因为这是此人的上司。

434
00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:16.180
Yes.
没错。

435
00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.080
So there's that.
所以情况就是这样。

436
00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:19.580
Here's what I was going to suggeSt.
这是我打算建议的方法。

437
00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:20.020
Okay.
好的。

438
00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:27.380
The next time, AR, you are speaking with your supervisor, I would ask about one of the very
下次，AR，当你和你的上司交谈时，我会问起你无意中听到的那些，

439
00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.900
personal things you overheard.
非常私人的事情之一。

440
00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:30.020
Wow.
哇。

441
00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:30.920
Yes.
是的。

442
00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:34.920
I would say, did you get that rash cleared up?
我会说，你的皮疹治好了吗？

443
00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:36.820
Or whatever it is.
或者诸如此类的话。

444
00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:37.420
Yeah.
没错。

445
00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:37.920
Yeah.
是啊。

446
00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:44.900
Another thing you could do is you could try the, like, the triangulate method, where you
你还可以尝试另一种方法，就是三角定位法，你可以，

447
00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:51.380
go to your supervisor and you say, there's a coworker who has taken a few personal calls
去找你的上司说，有位同事接了好几个私人电话，

448
00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:52.260
on speakerphone.
都开了免提。

449
00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:55.280
And I feel a little uncomfortable about it.
我对此感到有点不舒服。

450
00:16:55.400 --> 00:17:01.820
And I just didn't know, like, is there a way maybe you would write, like, a general email
我只是不知道，比如，有没有可能你写一封，比如，通用的邮件

451
00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:02.480
to the group?
对团队说吗？

452
00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:02.740
No.
不。

453
00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.220
You think they're going to know immediately?
你觉得他们会立刻发现吗？

454
00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:08.360
I think you have Pam brain right now from years of playing Pam.
我觉得你现在满脑子都是帕姆，毕竟演了这么多年的帕姆。

455
00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:12.440
This is how Pam would placate Michael, but it would always blow up in her face.
帕姆以前就是这样安抚迈克尔的，但结果总是会搞砸。

456
00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:13.080
No.
不。

457
00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:16.120
Then the boss is like, we need to have a meeting, everyone.
然后老板就会说，大家开个会吧。

458
00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:17.100
I don't know.
我不知道。

459
00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:17.680
I don't know.
我不知道。

460
00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:20.880
But I like your idea of mirroring.
但我喜欢你说的“镜像”策略。

461
00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:27.220
And then I like my idea of just, like, lean into it and be like, hey, how is the toe
我也喜欢我自己的想法，就是顺着话说，嘿，你的脚气

462
00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:27.620
fungus?
好了吗？

463
00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:29.620
Did you finally get that cleared up?
你终于治好了吗？

464
00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:30.780
Two ways to go.
有两种处理方式。

465
00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.900
Well, listen, I think we should take a break.
好吧，听着，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

466
00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:37.780
When we come back, we have a serious parking situation to discuss.
回来之后，我们要讨论一个严重的停车问题。

467
00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.100
Yes, we do.
确实如此。

468
00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.860
We are back, and our next letter is from CW in Minnesota.
我们回来了，下一封信来自明尼苏达州的CW。

469
00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:54.980
CW says this,
CW是这么说的：

470
00:17:55.720 --> 00:18:00.520
Since the pandemic started, I have been working from home, but my office recently announced
疫情开始后，我一直居家办公，但公司最近宣布

471
00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:03.420
that we are now required to come in two days a week.
我们现在每周必须去办公室两天。

472
00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:08.380
I would not be mad about this, but they make us pay for parking.
如果只是这样我倒不生气，但他们竟然还要我们付停车费。

473
00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.000
What?
什么？

474
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:09.100
What?
什么？

475
00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:10.260
Yeah.
是啊。

476
00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:14.560
And get this, the company owns the parking lot.
最绝的是，停车场还是公司自己的。

477
00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:15.340
No.
不会吧。

478
00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:15.900
Yes.
是真的。

479
00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:16.540
Come on.
别开玩笑了。

480
00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:19.060
And still makes the employees pay to park.
而且还要员工付钱停车。

481
00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.380
It costs $10 a day.
每天要10美元。

482
00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:22.440
That's BS.
这太扯了。

483
00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:25.160
That is over $1,000 a year.
那一年就是1000多美元。

484
00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:27.760
CW, I would be ticked off.
CW，我要是你会气炸的。

485
00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:28.560
Yes.
没错。

486
00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:29.680
There's more.
还没完呢。

487
00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:34.900
The parking ramp isn't even big enough for all the employees, so some people have to park
停车场甚至大到装不下所有员工的车，所以有些人不得不停在

488
00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:38.220
further away and walk 15 minutes to the office.
更远的地方，然后步行15分钟去办公室。

489
00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:41.640
See Kevin in chairmodel for my feelings on this.
看看《凯文的模特椅》那集，就知道我的感受了。

490
00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:42.660
Yes.
没错。

491
00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.180
This is crazy, right?
这太疯狂了，对吧？

492
00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:46.000
I should not have to pay to go to work.
我不应该为了上班还要付钱。

493
00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:46.920
Agree.
同意。

494
00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.300
I'm with CW on this.
我支持CW的看法。

495
00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:50.840
I think that's a load of crap.
我觉得这简直是胡扯。

496
00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:55.560
I mean, you're basically taking $1,000 out of your salary to park.
我的意思是，你基本上是从工资里扣掉1000美元来停车。

497
00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:56.880
That is BS.
这太扯了。

498
00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.040
Do you want to hear something?
你想听个东西吗？

499
00:18:58.280 --> 00:18:58.360
What?
什么？

500
00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.320
Do you want to hear why I connected with this question?
你想知道为什么我对这个问题感同身受吗？

501
00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:00.940
Yeah.
是啊。

502
00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:01.980
This happened to me.
这种事我也遇到过。

503
00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:06.820
I was working as an executive assistant in this big office building in downtown Los
我当时在洛杉矶市中心的一栋大办公楼里做行政助理。

504
00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:07.140
Angeles.
那栋楼有停车场，但公司只给高管支付停车费。

505
00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:14.380
It had a parking garage, but the company would only pay for the parking spaces of the executives.
这是他们薪酬待遇的一部分。

506
00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.920
It was part of their salary package.
我是按小时计薪的员工。

507
00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:18.900
I was an hourly worker.
我没有薪酬待遇包。

508
00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:20.700
I didn't have a salary package.
里面不包含停车费。

509
00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:21.860
It didn't include parking.
我不得不把车停在几个街区外的一个收费停车场，然后走大概10到15分钟的路。

510
00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:28.920
I had to park in a pay lot several blocks away and walk probably 10 or 15 minutes.
嗯哼。

511
00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:29.500
Mm-hmm.
有一次我老板要去度假，我就问他我能不能在他不在的时候用他的停车位。

512
00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:36.500
So one time when my boss was going to go on vacation, I asked if I could use his parking
我说，你不介意我用你的停车卡停在你的车位上吧？

513
00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.380
space while he was gone.
他当时就说，你不是已经在楼里停车了吗？

514
00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:41.580
I said, would you mind if I used your parking card and I parked in your space?
我说，没有，我没在楼里停车。

515
00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:45.020
And he was like, well, don't you already park here?
我停在第五街那边。

516
00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.660
And I said, no, I don't park here.
要走15分钟。

517
00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:50.420
I park down on 5th Street.
是啊。

518
00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.020
15 minutes away.
他当时就说，什么？

519
00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:51.340
Yeah.
值得称赞的是，当他发现我没能在楼里停车时，他让公司给了我一个停车位。

520
00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:52.380
He was like, what?
他们修改了政策。

521
00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:58.180
To his credit, when he found out that I did not get to park in the building, he made
那太棒了。

522
00:19:58.180 --> 00:19:59.700
the company give me a parking space.
因为他真的很棒。

523
00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:00.760
They changed the policy.
